      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠲᠢᠺ</unicode>
      <uighur>tik</uighur>
      <cyrillic>тэг</cyrillic>
      <transcript>TIG</transcript>
      <definition>[= teg, 1. T. thig[le] = S. bindu] n. Line, circular mark in writing; punctuation mark; zero, cipher, naught; small circle on top of a Tibetan or Mongolian letter in transcriptions from Sanskrit, indicating nasalization, as in the familiar Sanskrit word OM; emptiness; reed pen.</definition>
      <page>809</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠲᠢᠺ ᠤᠨ ᠤᠲᠠᠰᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>utasu</transcript>
          <definition> Carpenter's marking string.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠠᠰᠬ᠎ᠠ ᠲᠢᠺ</unicode>
          <transcript>asx-a -- </transcript>
          <definition> Crayon, slate-pencil.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠳᠤᠮᠳᠠ ᠲᠢᠺ</unicode>
          <transcript>dumda -- </transcript>
          <definition> Diameter, meridian.</definition>
        </example>
